{
 "set": "Maltster-published diastatic power",
 "note": "Every maltster figure behind data/fermentables, transcribed exactly as its publisher prints it, so that app/validate-diastatic.mjs can fail the build the moment a record disagrees with its own citation. This file exists because an audit found that 22 of the 23 diastatic-power figures this catalogue held were not the figure the cited document printed: seven differed from a number that was right there in the sheet, thirteen cited documents that carry no diastatic power at all, and two rested on withdrawn pages. Only Briess Brewers Malt matched. Nothing here is this project's opinion — where a maltster publishes no diastatic power, the malt is absent from this file rather than given a plausible one.",
 "generated": "2026-08-11",
 "units": {
  "diastaticPower": "°Lintner, which is the same scale as °ASBC. Maltsters publish on three scales; the printed figure and its unit are kept verbatim and the °Lintner equivalent is derived, so the arithmetic can be checked.",
  "alphaAmylase": "DU, dextrinizing units"
 },
 "conversions": {
  "wkToLintner": "°L = (°WK + 16) / 3.5",
  "iobToWk": "°WK = °IoB x 3.75",
  "verifiedBy": "Not taken from a homebrewing blog, which is where this relation is usually found and which cannot support a number here. Simpsons Malt publishes diastatic power for the same malt on all three scales, which makes the relation checkable against a maltster's own analysis. Across their eight malts that carry a diastatic power there are 15 (WK, published °Lintner) pairs spanning 75-300 °WK, and (°WK + 16) / 3.5 reproduces every published °Lintner figure to within 0.4. The IoB relation is exact on all four points: 150/40, 244/65, 300/80 and 75/20 are all precisely 3.75."
 },
 "shape": "malts[sourceKey][product].diastaticPower is one of {value}, {min,max}, {min,atLeast:true} for a '>n' floor, or {max,atMost:true} for a '<n' ceiling, always alongside the verbatim `published` string and its `unit`. Figures published in WK or IoB also carry lintnerValue/lintnerMin/lintnerMax. statedInWords marks a zero a maltster asserted in prose rather than in its analysis table. enzymeActivity is Weyermann's qualitative line, which is all they publish for all but one malt.",
 "sources": {
  "rahr-2026": {
   "publisher": "Rahr Malting Co.",
   "title": "Rahr Malting Co. product pages and per-product info sheets",
   "url": "https://rahrmaltingco.com/products/",
   "kind": "maltster product pages, each with a downloadable info-sheet PDF",
   "retrieved": "2026-08-11",
   "unit": "lintner",
   "read": "All 17 products enumerated from rahrmaltingco.com/product-sitemap.xml and fetched. Rahr prints diastatic power in °Lintner directly, so nothing here is converted. Six products carry no diastatic power and are recorded as absent rather than as zero."
  },
  "great-western-sell-sheets": {
   "publisher": "Great Western Malting",
   "title": "Great Western Malting sell sheets (typical analysis)",
   "url": "https://www.greatwesternmalting.com/products/",
   "kind": "maltster sell sheets, one PDF per product",
   "retrieved": "2026-08-11",
   "unit": "lintner",
   "read": "19 products enumerated from product-sitemap.xml; each product page's linked sell sheet was downloaded and read. Extracted with poppler's layout mode, NOT pdfminer: pdfminer drops the row labels on these sheets and leaves a bare column of numbers, which is exactly how a value gets attached to the wrong label. Four sheets were then read by eye against the parse. Nine sheets carry no diastatic power row."
  },
