   "kind": "maltster product catalogue",
   "retrieved": "2026-08-11",
   "unit": "wk",
   "read": "All 63 pages read by geometry. THE FINDING THAT MATTERS: exactly one page in the whole catalogue prints a \"Diastatic power\" row — Weyermann® Diastatic Barley Malt, min 300 WK. Every other malt's analysis table stops at viscosity, friability and glassy kernels. The per-product PRODUCT SPECIFICATION PDFs on weyermann.de carry no diastatic power either. What Weyermann does publish for every malt is a qualitative line, \"Enzyme activity: none | low | medium | high\", recorded below. Twenty-six malts are stated to have none, which is a published zero and is used as one."
  }
